1. Statutory Pay Systems. The rates of basic pay or salaries of\nthe statutory pay systems (as defined in 5 U.S.C. 5302(1)), as adjusted\nunder 5 U.S.C. 5303(a), in accordance with section 647(a) of the Treasury\nand General Government Appropriations Act, 1999, as incorporated in Divi-\nsion A, section 101(h) of Public Law 105–277, are set forth on the schedules\nattached hereto and made a part hereof:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"63 FR 68151 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 1 (lead-in)","sha256":"5547410c35bff7509524be6a7f19243e8271bbe1a16c079dc4f19c945ed95fcc","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1998-12-09/pdf/98-32953.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13106#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The General Schedule (5 U.S.C. 5332(a)) at Schedule 1;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"63 FR 68151 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 1(a)","sha256":"5547410c35bff7509524be6a7f19243e8271bbe1a16c079dc4f19c945ed95fcc","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1998-12-09/pdf/98-32953.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13106#sec1(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Foreign Service Schedule (22 U.S.C. 3963) atSchedule 2; and","original_source":{"page_or_item":"63 FR 68151 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 1(b)","sha256":"5547410c35bff7509524be6a7f19243e8271bbe1a16c079dc4f19c945ed95fcc","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1998-12-09/pdf/98-32953.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13106#sec1(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) The schedules for the Veterans Health Administrationof the Department\nof Veterans Affairs (38 U.S.C. 7306, 7404; section 301(a) of Public Law\n102–40) at Schedule 3.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"63 FR 68151 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 1(c)","sha256":"5547410c35bff7509524be6a7f19243e8271bbe1a16c079dc4f19c945ed95fcc","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1998-12-09/pdf/98-32953.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13106#sec1(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. Senior Executive Service. The rates of basic pay for senior executives\nin the Senior Executive Service, as adjusted under 5 U.S.C. 5382, are set\nforth on Schedule 4 attached hereto and made a part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"63 FR 68151 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 2","sha256":"5547410c35bff7509524be6a7f19243e8271bbe1a16c079dc4f19c945ed95fcc","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1998-12-09/pdf/98-32953.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13106#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. Executive Salaries. The rates of basic pay or salaries for the following\noffices and positions, which remain unchanged pursuant to section 621\nof the Treasury and General Government Appropriations Act, 1999, as incor-\nporated in Division A, section 101(h) of Public Law 105–277, are set forth\non the schedules attached hereto and made a part hereof:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"63 FR 68151 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 3 (lead-in)","sha256":"5547410c35bff7509524be6a7f19243e8271bbe1a16c079dc4f19c945ed95fcc","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1998-12-09/pdf/98-32953.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13106#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Executive Schedule (5 U.S.C. 5312–5318) at Schedule 5;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"63 FR 68151 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"5547410c35bff7509524be6a7f19243e8271bbe1a16c079dc4f19c945ed95fcc","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1998-12-09/pdf/98-32953.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13106#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Vice President (3 U.S.C. 104) and the Congress (2 U.S.C. 31)\nat Schedule 6; and","original_source":{"page_or_item":"63 FR 68151 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 3(b)","sha256":"5547410c35bff7509524be6a7f19243e8271bbe1a16c079dc4f19c945ed95fcc","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1998-12-09/pdf/98-32953.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13106#sec3(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Justices and judges (28 U.S.C. 5, 44(d), 135, 252, and 461(a)) at Schedule\n7.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"63 FR 68151 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 3(c)","sha256":"5547410c35bff7509524be6a7f19243e8271bbe1a16c079dc4f19c945ed95fcc","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1998-12-09/pdf/98-32953.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13106#sec3(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 4. Uniformed Services. Pursuant to sections 601 and 604 of Public\nLaw 105–85, the rates of monthly basic pay (37 U.S.C. 203(a)) for members\nof the uniformed services and the rate of monthly cadet or midshipman\npay (37 U.S.C. 203(c)) are set forth on Schedule 8 attached hereto and\nmade a part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"63 FR 68151 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 4","sha256":"5547410c35bff7509524be6a7f19243e8271bbe1a16c079dc4f19c945ed95fcc","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1998-12-09/pdf/98-32953.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13106#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Pursuant to section 5304\nof title 5, United States Code, and in accordance with section 647(a) of\nthe Treasury and General Government Appropriations Act, 1999, as incor-\nporated in Division A, section 101(h) of Public Law 105–277, locality-based\ncomparability payments shall be paid in accordance with Schedule 9 attached\nhereto and made a part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"63 FR 68151 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 5(a)","sha256":"5547410c35bff7509524be6a7f19243e8271bbe1a16c079dc4f19c945ed95fcc","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1998-12-09/pdf/98-32953.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13106#sec5(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Director of the Office of Personnel Management shall take such\nactions as may be necessary to implement these payments and to publish\nappropriate notice of such payments in the Federal Register.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"63 FR 68151 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 5(b)","sha256":"5547410c35bff7509524be6a7f19243e8271bbe1a16c079dc4f19c945ed95fcc","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1998-12-09/pdf/98-32953.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13106#sec5(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 6. Effective Dates. Schedule 8 is effective on January 1, 1999. The\nother schedules contained herein are effective on the first day of the first\napplicable pay period beginning on or after January 1, 1999.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"63 FR 68151 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 6","sha256":"5547410c35bff7509524be6a7f19243e8271bbe1a16c079dc4f19c945ed95fcc","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1998-12-09/pdf/98-32953.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13106#sec6","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 7. Prior Order Superseded. Executive Order 13071 of December 29,\n1997, is superseded.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"63 FR 68151 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 7","sha256":"5547410c35bff7509524be6a7f19243e8271bbe1a16c079dc4f19c945ed95fcc","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1998-12-09/pdf/98-32953.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13106#sec7","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 8. Delegation of a Federal Pay Administration Authority. Executive\nOrder 12748, as amended, is further amended in section 2(c) by deleting\n‘‘5304(h)’’ and inserting ‘‘5304(g)–(h)’’ in lieu thereof.","o